{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And the altar shall be most holy</b> — because they would also offer on it sacrifices of the holiest degree, he said this of it even though it was in the courtyard. And he also said of the Tabernacle (Exodus 40:9), \"And it shall be holy,\" for nothing is called \"most holy\" except the place of the dwelling of the ark, as it is stated (Exodus 26:33), \"And the veil shall separate for you between the holy and between the Holy of Holies.\" And it is possible that he said of the altar \"most holy\" because whatever touches it becomes sanctified, as he said, \"And the altar shall be most holy; whatever touches the altar shall become sanctified\" (Exodus 29:37)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:22:30.372488890Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}